<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M2-PER-SEC-BAR> a ns1:Unit ;
    rdfs:label "square metre per second bar" ;
    dcterms:description """\r
  The unit $\\textit{Square Metre per Second Bar}$ typically refers to a measure of fluid permeability in the\r
   context of materials science or engineering.\r
  It is the volume of fluid (in square metres) that can pass through a material in one second under a pressure difference of one bar. \r
  This unit is particularly important in fields such as petrophysics, hydrogeology, and materials engineering,\r
   where understanding the flow of fluids through porous media is crucial.\r
  A $Bar$ is not an SI unit but is a unit of pressure that is widely used in various scientific and engineering contexts.\r
  A bar is equal to $100,000\\ pascals\\(Pa)$, approximately equal to the atmospheric pressure on Earth at sea level.\r
  """^^ns1:LatexString ;
    ns1:conversionMultiplier 0.00001 ;
    ns1:conversionMultiplierSN 1e-05 ;
    ns1:hasDimensionVector <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L3I0M-1H0T1D0> ;
    ns1:hasQuantityKind <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Unknown> ;
    ns1:iec61360Code "0112/2///62720#UAB493" ;
    ns1:symbol "m²/(s·bar)" ;
    ns1:ucumCode "m2.s-1.bar-1"^^ns1:UCUMcs ;
    ns1:uneceCommonCode "G41" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit> .

<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M2-PER-SEC-K> a ns1:Unit ;
    rdfs:label "square metre per second kelvin" ;
    dcterms:description """\r
  The unit $\\textit{Square Metre per Second Kelvin}$ is a heat transfer coefficient that is area-dependent\r
   and varies with time and temperature difference. \r
  Heat transfer is typically defined in terms of watts per square meter per kelvin ($W/m^{2}K$),\r
   representing the rate of heat transfer across a surface per unit area per unit temperature difference.\r
  """^^ns1:LatexString ;
    ns1:conversionMultiplier 1.0 ;
    ns1:conversionMultiplierSN 1e+00 ;
    ns1:hasDimensionVector <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M0H-1T-1D0> ;
    ns1:hasQuantityKind <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Unknown> ;
    ns1:iec61360Code "0112/2///62720#UAA753",
        "0112/2///62720#UAD680" ;
    ns1:symbol "m²/(s·K)" ;
    ns1:ucumCode "m2.s-1.K-1"^^ns1:UCUMcs ;
    ns1:uneceCommonCode "G09" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit> .

<http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M2-PER-SEC-PA> a ns1:Unit ;
    rdfs:label "square metre per second pascal" ;
    dcterms:description """\r
  The unit $\\textit{Square Metre per Second Pascal}$, symbol $m^{2}/s\\cdot Pa$, is a measure of permeability, which describes the ability\r
   of a material to allow fluids to pass through it under a pressure gradient. \r
  It's particularly relevant in fields like hydrogeology, petroleum engineering, and civil engineering,\r
   where understanding fluid flow through porous materials is essential.\r
  """^^ns1:LatexString ;
    ns1:conversionMultiplier 1.0 ;
    ns1:conversionMultiplierSN 1e+00 ;
    ns1:hasDimensionVector <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L3I0M-1H0T1D0> ;
    ns1:hasQuantityKind <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Unknown> ;
    ns1:iec61360Code "0112/2///62720#UAB460" ;
    ns1:symbol "m²/(s·Pa)" ;
    ns1:ucumCode "m2.s-1.Pa-1"^^ns1:UCUMcs ;
    ns1:uneceCommonCode "M82" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit> .

