ns2:EnumerationKind a ns2:Class,
        ns2:EnumerationKind,
        sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "Enumeration kind" ;
    rdfs:comment """This is the encapsulating class for all EnumerationKinds. \r
  EnumerationKinds define the (closed) set of permissible values for a given purpose. \r
  For example, the DayOfWeek EnumerationKind enumerates the days of the week and allows no other values.\r
\r
EnumerationKinds are arranged in a class hierarchy tree, with the root class named EnumerationKind. Each subclass is named \r
starting with its immediate superclass, followed by a hyphen and a name that is unique among the sibling classes. \r
Each class is also an instance of itself. This unusual modeling pattern was used to achieve:\r
\r
- The ability to set an EnumerationKind value that is more general, or not yet fully specified \r
at the time of modeling, such as s223:Electricity-AC without having to state exactly what voltage or frequency it is.\r
\r
- The ability to use the sh:class SHACL predicate at any level in the EnumerationKind hierarchy \r
to constrain a value in the s223 specification, even if it is a more general one such as s223:Electricity-AC in the above example.\r
\r
Certain validation constraints exist in the standard that evaluate compatibility of EnumerationKinds. \r
Two values are deemed compatible if they are the same, if one is a direct ancestor (or descendant) of the other, \r
or if they are mixtures sharing at least one constituent.""" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns2:Concept .

